## Why this exists

My close-out handoff carried two wrong figures. The sent handoff is not edited, so the correction is
here. One of the two changes the reword list, which is why this goes to you rather than staying in my
status file.

## 1. `a9afb740` is NOT exempt from the reword — add it to the list

I wrote *"C9e's own message is written token-free."* **That is false.** `a9afb740`'s body contains
`N2 N3 N7 N8 W1 W4 U2 T1.4` and `PR-2 C2, C7, C10, C11, C6e, D-b`.

They are there only as the **object of description** — the message explains which class of shorthand
it removed, and enumerates it. That is a mention, not a use, and it is the same shape as `4fb49ac6`.
But §4a has no quoting exemption, and a `main` reader meeting that enumeration in `git log` hits
exactly the problem §4a exists to prevent. So it should be reworded like the rest, not recorded as an
exception.

The reword is cheap and lossless: the message already says **"plan-item labels"** and **"per-commit
labels"** one clause earlier, so the two parenthesised enumerations can simply be dropped. The
"T1-ols" paragraph and `throughput/constants.go:129` stay — that is a real in-repo identifier and its
whole point is that it is not a plan token.

## 2. The ledger denominator is 25, not 24

`git rev-list 075a208e..HEAD | wc -l` = **25**. I reported "21 of 24".

The numerator is **21 under the reviewer's rule and 22 under mine**, and the single disputed message
is `b106b929`, whose only hit is *"PR-1's Test 9"*. A PR reference resolves from `main` — the same
reasoning that kept `#1513` in `optimizer_invariant7_test.go` — so **21 of 25** is the better figure
and the one to carry.

## Findings 60, 61, 63 — no work for this branch, nothing committed

- **60** is a reviewer-instrument defect (the sweep filter excluded test descriptions, which §4a names
  explicitly). Nothing on my side.
- **61** is inherited: three of the 8 inherited sites carry no token at all, so no pattern-based
  sweep can span the class. Confirms the method; no action here.
- **63** reclassifies one row of the inherited list I gave you, and the reclassification is right —
  I checked it rather than taking it. `docs/developer-guide/throughput-analyzer.md:609` links
  `../saturation-scaling-config.md`; from `docs/developer-guide/` that resolves to
  `docs/saturation-scaling-config.md`, which is **absent**, while
  `docs/developer-guide/saturation-scaling-config.md` exists. So it is a **broken relative link** —
  drop the `../` — and belongs with `cmd/main.go:167`, not with the plans-branch-citation rows. Still
  inherited, still present in `upstream/main`, still not PR-2's to change.

